{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-7dd35da7-1d3f-42f3-852c-7867cd1683bb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9400c1799f11ec3d","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-yaps0um6/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E001.md","content":"# Standardize reconciliation error logging in the rhods-operator manager binary\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic converts message-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs across all reconciliation error logs in the rhods-operator manager binary, migrates the DSCInitialization (DSCI) controller from non-standard key names to the standard camelCase convention, and adds `resourceKind` as a structured field to every controller tier and action file. It also adds a CI lint rule that prevents regression by flagging new `log.Error` calls that embed resource identity in message text or omit the required structured fields.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths across the manager binary's five controller tiers — the DataScienceCluster (DSC) controller, the 8 component controllers (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, SparkOperator, Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI), the module controller with its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX, Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator), the DSCI controller, and the 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) — and produce a coverage checklist of all call sites.\n- Convert every call site that embeds resource name or namespace in the message string (e.g., `log.Error(err, \"failed to reconcile Dashboard 'example' in namespace 'redhat-ods-applications'\")`) to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`), removing the redundant identity from the message text.\n- Migrate the DSCI controller's structured field names from `Request.Name` / `DSCInitialization` to the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`).\n- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to reconciliation error logs in the service controllers, the module controller and its 8 module handlers, the DSC controller, and the 8 component controllers (for the latter two, `resourceKind` enables cross-controller queries even though the reconciler name implies the kind).\n- Handle cluster-scoped resources (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization) correctly: emit `name` and `resourceKind`, with `namespace` omitted or set to empty string — never a spurious value.\n- Add a CI lint rule or static analysis check, covering both the manager and cloudmanager binaries, that flags any `log.Error` call embedding name/namespace in message text or missing the required structured fields.\n- Add unit tests that parse test logger output and assert field presence and correctness.\n- Coordinate with SRE/Support to identify text-based alert rules that rely on message-string patterns, and perform a before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error confirming that structured fields appear and the log consumer (Loki) ingests both formats without configuration changes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A CI lint rule or static analysis check reports zero `log.Error` calls in the manager binary with resource name or namespace embedded in the message text.\n- Unit tests assert that DSCI error logs contain the standard field names (`name`, `namespace`), and a codebase grep confirms no references to `Request.Name` / `DSCInitialization` as structured field names remain; the DSCI key transition lands in a single release.\n- Unit tests parsing test logger output assert `resourceKind` is present with the correct value for each of the 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup).\n- Unit tests assert `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` are present with correct values across all 15 action files (8 component: `components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`; 3 service: `services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`; 1 DSC: `datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`; 3 module: `modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`).\n- Unit tests assert the module controller's error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` across all 8 module handlers.\n- Unit tests assert DSC and component controller error logs include `resourceKind` for cross-controller queryability.\n- Unit tests confirm cluster-scoped resources do not emit a spurious namespace value.\n- A before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error confirms structured fields appear and a log consumer ingests both formats without configuration changes; text-based alert rules identified with SRE/Support are updated or confirmed unaffected before merge.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): all rhods-operator reconciliation error logs that embed resource name or namespace in message strings are converted to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`) — manager-binary call sites.\n- HLR-2 (P0): DSCI controller migrated from non-standard key names to camelCase convention.\n- HLR-3 (P0): service controller reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind`.\n- HLR-4 (P0): all action file error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` across all 4 tiers (15 action files).\n- HLR-6 (P0): module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` (8 module handlers).\n- HLR-7 (P1, bundled): DSC and component controller reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind` — bundled because it edits the same `log.Error` call sites as the HLR-1/HLR-4 conversion in the same controllers; the field is added in the same mechanical pass and splitting would double-touch every call site.\n\n## Risks\n\n- **Missed error paths** across the 5 controller tiers and 15 action files — mitigated by grep/static analysis to identify all call sites, a tracked coverage checklist, and the CI lint rule.\n- **Log consumer regression**: text-based alerts may break when message strings change — mitigated by the before/after ingestion comparison and SRE/Support coordination captured in the acceptance criteria.\n- **DSCI key name migration breaks existing queries** filtering on `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` — mitigated by landing the transition in a single release, release-notes documentation, and before/after query examples (documentation deliverable tracked in the convention guideline work).\n\n## Open Questions\n\n- Whether the convention should include fields beyond `name`/`namespace`/`resourceKind` (e.g., reconciliation attempt count, error category) is a PM / Observability decision. It is additive to the same call sites and does not change the conversion approach; if adopted, the fields are added to the same call sites before or during this work.\n- The actual percentage of log calls embedding resource identity (SME estimate: 75%) is confirmed by this epic's audit step; the conversion proceeds over whatever sites are found.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":52575,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8bcd7d7142debc9e","agent_id":"acc070392a2e429ac","session_id":"a719d0dc-396c-46d9-8e0e-5a6d9af711e0","uuid":"c04dfa14-f632-4fe3-a670-eaede8a94521","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:18:12.106Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010"}
