{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-844cad78f02af48e","type":"tool_result","content":"must-gather.md\nodh-observability.md\nPLATFORM.md\nrhods-operator.md\n---\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-yaps0um6/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/must-gather.md:80:| rhods-operator | API (Subscription lookup) | Required | Detects operator namespace and RHOAI version via ClusterServiceVersion |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-yaps0um6/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/odh-observability.md:16:**Detailed**: odh-observability implements a controller-runtime operator that reconciles a cluster-scoped `Monitoring` custom resource (`services.platform.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1`) to deploy and configure a complete observability stack for RHOAI. The operator manages Prometheus-based metrics collection with configurable storage and retention, distributed tracing through the Tempo operator with S3/GCS/PV storage backends, and usage log collection via LokiStack with OpenTelemetry collectors. It deploys kube-rbac-proxy sidecars for authenticated Prometheus access through SubjectAccessReview-based authorization and creates OpenShift Routes for external TLS exposure. The operator uses odh-platform-utilities for server-side-apply deployment via the `deploy.Deployer`, platform detection, and shared API types including the `PlatformObject` interface for standardized status and condition management across RHOAI services. A mutating admission webhook injects monitoring labels into PodMonitor and ServiceMonitor resources to ensure consistent metrics collection across data science workloads. [source: api/v1alpha1/monitoring_types.go:20-41, cmd/main.go:40-134, internal/controller/resources/data-science-prometheus-cluster-proxy.tmpl.yaml:58-93, Dockerfiles/Dockerfile.konflux:19]\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-yaps0um6/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/odh-observability.md:20:odh-observability follows a reconciler pattern built on controller-runtime, with a single `MonitoringReconciler` watching the cluster-scoped `Monitoring` CR and managing a broad set of dependent resources through server-side apply. The operator uses odh-platform-utilities' `deploy.Deployer` configured with SSA mode and ordered apply, which renders Go templates into Kubernetes manifests and applies them declaratively without conflict with Helm or other field managers. [source: cmd/main.go:109-114]\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-yaps0um6/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/odh-observability.md:50:| cmd | Go controller-runtime operator | cmd |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-yaps0um6/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/odh-observability.md:99:| sigs.k8s.io/controller-runtime | v0.23.3 | Yes | runtime-framework | runtime-framework |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-yaps0um6/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/odh-observability.md:101:| controller-runtime | 0.23.3 | Yes | Unknown | Operator framework |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-yaps0um6/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/odh-observability.md:205:| **TLS configuration** | Controller-runtime default TLS for webhook server; kube-rbac-proxy handles proxy TLS with explicit cert/key args | cmd/main.go:97-100, internal/controller/resources/data-science-prometheus-cluster-proxy.tmpl.yaml:85-89 |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-yaps0um6/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:16:Red Hat OpenShift AI (RHOAI) 3.6-ea.1 is a comprehensive AI/ML platform deployed on OpenShift Container Platform through the Operator Lifecycle Manager (OLM). The platform is orchestrated by rhods-operator, which manages the lifecycle of all platform components through a hierarchy of custom resources — DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization, and per-component CRDs. Each major capability (model serving, pipelines, distributed workloads, notebooks, model registry, training, observability, guardrails, and models-as-a-service) is implemented by a dedicated module operator or controller that watches its component CR and reconciles downstream Kubernetes resources using kustomize-based manifest rendering through the shared odh-platform-utilities framework.\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-yaps0um6/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:18:The platform ingress architecture is in active transition. The rhods-operator Gateway service controller provisions a central `data-science-gateway` using Gateway API (GatewayClass, Gateway, HTTPRoutes) while maintaining backward compatibility through OpenShift Routes. kube-auth-proxy provides OIDC-authenticated access to the dashboard, and the Gateway controller conditionally integrates with Istio by dynamically creating EnvoyFilter and DestinationRule resources when Istio CRDs are detected. Models-as-a-Service introduces a parallel ingress path through Kuadrant AuthPolicy enforcement with API key, TokenReview, and optional OIDC JWT authentication at the Gateway level. Model-registry-operator implements dual ingress (Gateway API HTTPRoutes and OpenShift Routes) with kube-rbac-proxy sidecar authentication on backend pods.\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-yaps0um6/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:27:rhods-operator\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-yaps0um6/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:65:**rhods-operator** is the platform root: it owns all component CRDs (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, SparkOperator, Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI) and three service controllers (Auth, Gateway, Monitoring) that manage cross-cutting platform infrastructure. Every component operator depends on rhods-operator for activation and lifecycle management.\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-yaps0um6/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:67:**kserve** is the most connected serving component with 13 CRDs, 4 independent controller binaries (manager, llmisvc, localmodel, kserve-module), and integration with Gateway API, KEDA, cert-manager, Istio, and the Gateway API Inference Extension. Both rhods-operator and model-registry depend on it.\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-yaps0um6/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:79:| CRD-based orchestration | rhods-operator, kserve, odh-model-controller, models-as-a-service, kuberay, kueue-operator, trainer-operator, workbenches-operator, spark-operator, model-registry-operator, feast-module-operator, mlflow-operator, ai-gateway-operator, ogx-k8s-operator, trustyai-service-operator, data-science-pipelines-operator, mcp-lifecycle-operator, mcp-lifecycle-module-operator, llm-d-batch-gateway-operator | Each component defines cluster-scoped CRDs watched by the platform operator; component operators reconcile their own CRDs into namespace-scoped workloads |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-yaps0um6/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:81:| Gateway API routing | rhods-operator, models-as-a-service, model-registry-operator, kserve (llmisvc), odh-model-controller | HTTPRoute resources reference the data-science-gateway for authenticated external access; components own their routes and bind to a shared gateway |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-yaps0um6/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:82:| kube-rbac-proxy sidecar | kserve, odh-model-controller, model-registry-operator, rhods-operator (monitoring proxies), odh-dashboard | TLS-terminating authentication proxy injected as a sidecar; validates tokens via Kubernetes TokenReview/SubjectAccessReview |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-yaps0um6/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:84:| Platform TLS profile alignment | rhods-operator, kserve, odh-model-controller, model-registry-operator, workbenches-operator, trainer | Operators read the OpenShift APIServer TLS security profile and apply matching cipher suites and minimum TLS version to their own endpoints |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-yaps0um6/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:93:| redhat-ods-operator / opendatahub-operator-system | Operator namespace | rhods-operator |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-yaps0um6/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:98:| models-as-a-service | MaaS namespace | maas-api, maas-controller; rhods-operator Auth controller watches this namespace |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-yaps0um6/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:99:| kuadrant-system | Kuadrant infrastructure | Authorino/Kuadrant controllers; rhods-operator Auth controller watches this namespace |\n/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-yaps0um6/.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/PLATFORM.md:105:| data-science-gateway (openshift-ingress) | rhods-operator Gateway service controller | HTTPRoutes from models-as-a-service, model-