lert rules identified with SRE/Support are updated or confirmed unaffected **before merge**\" — the alert-rule-update half depends on SRE/Support action and turnaround. The before/after verification belongs in the ACs; the external-team update dependency belongs in Risks/Notes (where it already appears) rather than as a merge-blocking AC.\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\nThe combined epic set accounts for the full strategy scope: all five controller tiers plus cloudmanager in E001/E002, the 15 action files across 4 tiers, DSCI key migration, cluster-scoped resource handling, the CI lint rule, the SRE/Support coordination and before/after log-consumer verification (Backwards Compatibility NFR), and the complete documentation deliverable in E003 (contribution guideline with required fields/camelCase rationale/three-problem diagnosis/before/after examples, DSCI migration guide in release notes, external publication per overlay 0008 — matching the strategy's \"Design doc: To be created\" content list). All four strategy risks are carried into epic Risks/Notes; all four open questions are explicitly dispositioned; the effort-estimate work items all land in an epic. A docs-authoring epic exists (E003), satisfying Rule 11 even though the strategy's Documentation Support gate reads \"Pending human review\" rather than \"Yes\". The Performance NFR requires no verification per the strategy itself, so its absence from ACs is correct, not a silent drop. No conditional branches are needed — no bounded-outcome uncertainty exists in the strategy.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45290,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0910200606dfcc7","agent_id":"ad742ce4c46929491","session_id":"a719d0dc-396c-46d9-8e0e-5a6d9af711e0","uuid":"2b802416-5a81-4d07-b03a-d66be5c85548","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:23:11.948Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8010 dec