{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8922f3ee19a2b8a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n3\ttitle: Standardize reconciliation error logging in the rhods-operator manager binary\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Standardize reconciliation error logging in the rhods-operator manager binary\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic converts message-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs across all reconciliation error logs in the rhods-operator manager binary, migrates the DSCInitialization (DSCI) controller from non-standard key names to the standard camelCase convention, and adds `resourceKind` as a structured field to every controller tier and action file. It also adds a CI lint rule that prevents regression by flagging new `log.Error` calls that embed resource identity in message text or omit the required structured fields.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths across the manager binary's five controller tiers — the DataScienceCluster (DSC) controller, the 8 component controllers (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, SparkOperator, Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI), the module controller with its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX, Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator), the DSCI controller, and the 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) — and produce a coverage checklist of all call sites.\n38\t- Convert every call site that embeds resource name or namespace in the message string (e.g., `log.Error(err, \"failed to reconcile Dashboard 'example' in namespace 'redhat-ods-applications'\")`) to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`), removing the redundant identity from the message text.\n39\t- Migrate the DSCI controller's structured field names from `Request.Name` / `DSCInitialization` to the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`).\n40\t- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to reconciliation error logs in the service controllers, the module controller and its 8 module handlers, the DSC controller, and the 8 component controllers (for the latter two, `resourceKind` enables cross-controller queries even though the reconciler name implies the kind).\n41\t- Handle cluster-scoped resources (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization) correctly: emit `name` and `resourceKind`, with `namespace` omitted or set to empty string — never a spurious value.\n42\t- Add a CI lint rule or static analysis check, covering both the manager and cloudmanager binaries, that flags any `log.Error` call embedding name/namespace in message text or missing the required structured fields.\n43\t- Add unit tests that parse test logger output and assert field presence and correctness.\n44\t- Coordinate with SRE/Support to identify text-based alert rules that rely on message-string patterns, and perform a before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error confirming that structured fields appear and the log consumer (Loki) ingests both formats without configuration changes.\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- A CI lint rule or static analysis check reports zero `log.Error` calls in the manager binary with resource name or namespace embedded in the message text.\n49\t- Unit tests assert that DSCI error logs contain the standard field names (`name`, `namespace`), and a codebase grep confirms no references to `Request.Name` / `DSCInitialization` as structured field names remain; the DSCI key transition lands in a single release.\n50\t- Unit tests parsing test logger output assert `resourceKind` is present with the correct value for each of the 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup).\n51\t- Unit tests assert `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` are present with correct values across all 15 action files (8 component: `components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`; 3 service: `services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`; 1 DSC: `datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`; 3 module: `modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`).\n52\t- Unit tests assert the module controller's error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` across all 8 module handlers.\n53\t- Unit tests assert DSC and component controller error logs include `resourceKind` for cross-controller queryability.\n54\t- Unit tests confirm cluster-scoped resources do not emit a spurious namespace value.\n55\t- A before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error confirms structured fields appear and a log consumer ingests both formats without configuration changes; text-based alert rules identified with SRE/Support are updated or confirmed unaffected before merge.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- HLR-1 (P0): all rhods-operator reconciliation error logs that embed resource name or namespace in message strings are converted to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`) — manager-binary call sites.\n60\t- HLR-2 (P0): DSCI controller migrated from non-standard key names to camelCase convention.\n61\t- HLR-3 (P0): service controller reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind`.\n62\t- HLR-4 (P0): all action file error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` across all 4 tiers (15 action files).\n63\t- HLR-6 (P0): module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` (8 module handlers).\n64\t- HLR-7 (P1, bundled): DSC and component controller reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind` — bundled because it edits the same `log.Error` call sites as the HLR-1/HLR-4 conversion in the same controllers; the field is added in the same mechanical pass and splitting would double-touch every call site.\n65\t\n66\t## Risks\n67\t\n68\t- **Missed error paths** across the 5 controller tiers and 15 action files — mitigated by grep/static analysis to identify all call sites, a tracked coverage checklist, and the CI lint rule.\n69\t- **Log consumer regression**: text-based alerts may break when message strings change — mitigated by the before/after ingestion comparison and SRE/Support coordination captured in the acceptance criteria.\n70\t- **DSCI key name migration breaks existing queries** filtering on `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` — mitigated by landing the transition in a single release, release-notes documentation, and before/after query examples (documentation deliverable tracked in the convention guideline work).\n71\t\n72\t## Open Questions\n73\t\n74\t- Whether the convention should include fields beyond `name`/`namespace`/`resourceKind` (e.g., reconciliation attempt count, error category) is a PM / Observability decision. It is additive to the same call sites and does not change the conversion approach; if adopted, the fields are added to the same call sites before or during this work.\n75\t- The actual percentage of log calls embedding resource identity (SME estimate: 75%) is confirmed by this epic's audit step; the conversion proceeds over whatever sites are found.\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-893ab11fe4a7474e","agent_id":"a9f47c0b15b1784b5","session_id":"a719d0dc-396c-46d9-8e0e-5a6d9af711e0","uuid":"ae112a36-7a68-433c-b2b7-4c77af11490a","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:24:39.061Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8922f3ee19a2b8a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
