{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0aac134ea9144f0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n3\ttitle: Standardize reconciliation error logging in the rhods-operator cloudmanager\n4\t  binary\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n6\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n7\tteam: ODH Operator team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: 1\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Standardize reconciliation error logging in the rhods-operator cloudmanager binary\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic applies the structured reconciliation log convention to the rhods-operator cloudmanager binary — the companion binary that handles multi-cloud infrastructure dependencies on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (AWS EKS, Azure AKS, CoreWeave). Its three reconciliation controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) are built on the shared reconciler pattern and already receive `name` and `namespace` from controller-runtime's request logger; the remaining work is converting message-embedded resource identity in error paths to structured key-value pairs and adding `resourceKind`.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths of the three cloudmanager controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine), producing a coverage checklist.\n39\t- Convert every call site that embeds resource name or namespace in the message string to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`), removing the redundant identity from the message text.\n40\t- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to all cloudmanager reconciliation error logs (the kind is not implied by the shared reconciler, so this is a functional requirement here, not just a queryability enhancement).\n41\t- Add unit tests that parse test logger output and assert field presence and correctness for each controller.\n42\t- Perform a before/after log output comparison confirming the production log consumer stack on cloud deployments (e.g., CloudWatch) ingests both formats without configuration changes.\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- Unit tests assert `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` are present with correct values in test logger output for each of the three cloudmanager controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine).\n47\t- The audit checklist is complete: zero `log.Error` call sites with resource name or namespace embedded in message text remain in cloudmanager reconciliation error paths.\n48\t- A before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error confirms structured fields appear and the log consumer ingests both formats without configuration changes.\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- HLR-5 (P0): all cloudmanager controller (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) reconciliation error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields.\n53\t\n54\t## Notes\n55\t\n56\t- Cloudmanager is deployed only on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (AWS EKS, Azure AKS, CoreWeave), so its impact scope is narrower than the manager binary's. Whether this work lands in the same release as the manager-binary conversion or in a subsequent release is a PM / ODH Operator team scheduling decision; it does not change the work itself, which is why it is planned as an independently schedulable unit.\n57\t- The shared reconciler already provides `name`/`namespace` via controller-runtime's request logger, so no key-name migration is needed here — only embedded-identity conversion and `resourceKind`.\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-893ab11fe4a7474e","agent_id":"a9f47c0b15b1784b5","session_id":"a719d0dc-396c-46d9-8e0e-5a6d9af711e0","uuid":"2670d3df-07b0-4764-a774-906e921e2cc5","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:24:39.771Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0aac134ea9144f0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
