{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d446cedb17faf5b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E003\n3\ttitle: Document the structured reconciliation log convention and publish for external\n4\t  adoption\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n6\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n7\tteam: ODH Operator team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P1\n10\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n14\tai_signals:\n15\t  change_specificity: 1\n16\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n17\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n18\t  existing_foundation: 0\n19\t  open_questions: 0\n20\t  external_dependency: -1\n21\t  human_process_gates: 0\n22\t  repo_access: 1\n23\t  architecture_claims: 1\n24\tinvestigation_signals: null\n25\tai_implementability: Medium\n26\tai_implementability_score: 2\n27\tjira_key: null\n28\tbranch: null\n29\tgated_by: null\n30\tgate_failure_impact: null\n31\t---\n32\t# Document the structured reconciliation log convention and publish for external adoption\n33\t\n34\t## Description\n35\t\n36\tThis epic authors and publishes the structured reconciliation log field convention as a contribution guideline: the required fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`), the camelCase naming rationale, and the three-problem diagnosis (message-embedded identity, non-standard DSCI keys, missing `resourceKind`). It also publishes the convention for voluntary adoption by external operator teams (the Cluster Observability Operator team's Loki Operator and Tempo Operator) per platform policy, and documents the DSCI key-name migration in release notes.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\tContent outline of the guideline and related documentation:\n41\t\n42\t- A contribution guideline for new controller development specifying:\n43\t  - Required structured fields: `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`.\n44\t  - camelCase naming rationale (alignment with controller-runtime's structured log key conventions).\n45\t  - The three-problem diagnosis: message-embedded resource identity, non-standard DSCI key names (`Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization`), and missing `resourceKind`.\n46\t  - Before/after code examples for converting message-embedded identity to structured key-value pairs.\n47\t  - Cluster-scoped resource handling (`namespace` omitted or empty, never spurious).\n48\t- A DSCI key migration guide with before/after query examples, published in the release notes so operators using Loki/CloudWatch queries on the old field names can transition in the same release.\n49\t- Publication of the convention as a specification for external operator adoption (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator), on a voluntary basis per platform policy (overlay 0008 — RHOAI does not install, manage, or control external operator dependencies).\n50\t- Tracking issues filed in the external operator projects (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator) so adoption is visible and followable, accepting that adoption itself is best-effort.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- The contribution guideline exists and specifies the required fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`), the camelCase naming rationale, and the three-problem diagnosis.\n55\t- The guideline includes before/after code examples for converting message-embedded identity to structured key-value pairs, and a DSCI key migration guide with before/after query examples.\n56\t- The guideline is technically reviewed against the implemented logging changes in both the manager and cloudmanager binaries (the documented convention matches what the code actually emits, verified by the reviewers against the merged changes).\n57\t- The DSCI key migration is documented in release notes with before/after query examples.\n58\t- The convention is published for external operator adoption and tracking issues are filed in the Loki Operator and Tempo Operator projects.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- HLR-8 (P1): document the convention as a contribution guideline for new controller development and publish for external operator adoption.\n63\t\n64\t## Notes\n65\t\n66\t- External adoption by the COO team is voluntary per platform policy (overlay 0008); the RFE approval comment explicitly confirms this treatment. This epic's deliverable is the published convention and filed tracking issues — adoption itself is outside RHOAI's control and is not an acceptance criterion.\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-893ab11fe4a7474e","agent_id":"a9f47c0b15b1784b5","session_id":"a719d0dc-396c-46d9-8e0e-5a6d9af711e0","uuid":"5c1f10a5-0db0-4512-b560-e9c3e5b17792","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:24:40.438Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d446cedb17faf5b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
